- T1 receives the first real P3 label access;
- daemon-pinned code derives the allowed outcomes under the frozen contract;
- T1 is sealed before W1 may receive labels.

T1 continuation:
- REPLICATION_SUPPORTED -> W1 allowed;
- REPLICATION_FAILED -> W1 allowed;
- EVIDENCE_INSUFFICIENT_CURRENT_COHORT -> W1 allowed;
- TEST_VOIDED -> STOP, W1 forbidden.

Wave-1:
- exactly 174 frozen candidates;
- exact frozen order;
- no scientific early stop;
- no return-driven mutation;
- no partial candidate diagnostics to the LLM/orchestrator;
- resource exhaustion only yields same-wave checkpoint/resume;
- full wave must seal before H0 landscape interpretation.

## 0.7 Stop rule

At every stage, only the next unresolved gate is in scope.

If a gate fails:
- stop at that gate;
- capture expected predicate, observed predicate, command/status, and receipts;
- do not open a broad audit.

