# Part 5 — Fable harness design

## 5.1 Main-agent law

The main Cloud Fable agent is a thin router.

Every task requiring:
- reasoning;
- analysis;
- judgment;
- source/code interpretation;
- plan generation;
- command construction;
- report writing;
- result synthesis

must be delegated with:

`run_subagent(model="claude_fable_5")`

The main agent may only:
- read stage objective files;
- invoke subagents;
- wait;
- read their saved files;
- pass exact files/unmodified output forward;
- share files.

## 5.2 Single-writer law

Read-only review may be parallel.

Mutation is strictly serial.

At most one subagent may mutate:
- user/group/SSH/sudo state;
- `/etc/p5`;
- `/opt/p5`;
- production Research Memory;
- authority state;
- trial state;
- result/seal state.

Never run "reviewer" and "executor" both mutating the same gate.

## 5.3 Stage objectives

S0: fresh-session canonical state reconstruction.

S1: independent-admin Phase A coordinator (orders 2-4).

S2: fresh-k3 PRETRUST verifier (order 5).

S3: owner TCB signing-request coordinator.

S4: independent-admin Phase B deploy verifier/coordinator (orders 6-7).

S5: fresh-k3 final verifier (order 8).

S6: owner C/D/root coordinator.

S7: post-root A/B/T1/W1 executor.

Each objective is provided under `STAGE_OBJECTIVES/`.

## 5.4 No speculative execution

A subagent may not prepare the next mutating command on the assumption that the current gate
will pass if doing so risks using stale state.

Each stage must read the receipt/state produced by the previous stage.

